{"candidate_id":"figure-analysis:Figure6:dd21e64209d01755","artifact_id":"Figure6","visual_type":"plot","description":"Three side-by-side case-study boxes compare baseline and learned behavior for Formula, HumanEval, and GPQA Diamond tasks. The figure presents two positive flips (formula and executable-code tasks) and one representative negative flip (knowledge-intensive QA).","components":[{"name":"Formula: unit scale","role":"case-study panel","visual_evidence":"Left green box describes computing free cash flow, a baseline subtraction error, and a learned dollar-scale numeric answer."},{"name":"HumanEval: executable body","role":"case-study panel","visual_evidence":"Center blue box describes completing a function, a baseline missing an intended return statement, and a learned executable function body."},{"name":"GPQA Diamond: knowledge underweighted","role":"case-study panel","visual_evidence":"Right tan box describes selecting the densest Earth-like exoplanet, contrasting a rocky-planet prior with learned density reasoning and an Earth-baseline selection."},{"name":"Formula baseline","role":"baseline behavior","visual_evidence":"The left panel states that the baseline reverses the subtraction and retains the million-scale decimal, producing a negative value."},{"name":"Formula learned","role":"learned behavior","visual_evidence":"The left panel states that the learned behavior applies the formula in dollars and emits the strict numeric answer 400000.00."},{"name":"HumanEval baseline","role":"baseline behavior","visual_evidence":"The center panel states that the baseline writes a bare expression without the required intended return statement."},{"name":"HumanEval learned","role":"learned behavior","visual_evidence":"The center panel states that the learned behavior produces an executable function body with an accumulator and return."},{"name":"GPQA Diamond baseline","role":"baseline behavior","visual_evidence":"The right panel states that the baseline uses a rocky-planet prior in which higher mass increases self-compression and density."},{"name":"GPQA Diamond learned","role":"learned behavior","visual_evidence":"The right panel states that the learned behavior performs formulaic density reasoning, treats the same composition as constant density, and selects the Earth baseline."}],"relationships":[{"source_component":"Formula: unit scale","relation":"contains baseline behavior","target_component":"Formula baseline"},{"source_component":"Formula: unit scale","relation":"contains learned behavior","target_component":"Formula learned"},{"source_component":"HumanEval: executable body","relation":"contains baseline behavior","target_component":"HumanEval baseline"},{"source_component":"HumanEval: executable body","relation":"contains learned behavior","target_component":"HumanEval learned"},{"source_component":"GPQA Diamond: knowledge underweighted","relation":"contains baseline behavior","target_component":"GPQA Diamond baseline"},{"source_component":"GPQA Diamond: knowledge underweighted","relation":"contains learned behavior","target_component":"GPQA Diamond learned"}],"findings":["The visual compares baseline and learned outputs across three task types rather than showing quantitative axes or plotted measurements.","Formula and HumanEval panels depict improvements in procedure, formatting, or executability.","The GPQA Diamond panel depicts a representative negative flip, where learned reasoning underweights domain knowledge.","The figure caption says the boxes summarize task behavior rather than reproducing raw inputs."],"citations":[{"section_id":"sec-1~42","path_id":"1~42","quote":"Figure 6: Representative case-study flips. The boxes summarize task behavior rather than reproducing raw inputs; representative learned prompt and output excerpts are provided in Appendix A."},{"section_id":"sec-3.7.","path_id":"3.7.","quote":"Figure 6 shows two positive flips and one representative negative flip."},{"section_id":"sec-3.7.","path_id":"3.7.","quote":"For executable programs and formula-grounded computation, feedback teaches a better procedure: preserve the interface, handle edge cases, respect units, and emit a parseable final answer."},{"section_id":"sec-3.7.","path_id":"3.7.","quote":"For knowledge-intensive QA, the learned prompt often strengthens generic reasoning and answer-comparison behavior rather than adding the specific missing knowledge."}],"confidence":0.98,"provenance":{"image_sha256":"42c0c4730128fcd91ca2775a830a7247bf0699ef307712e4e90b4131f0cc3982","context_sha256":"2cfae7b2e3a348507554b5de44785389e4baca42b18f3c2cce1d95306846a755","route_id":"figure-qa-luna","protocol":"openai_chat_completions","requested_model":"cx/gpt-5.6-luna","resolved_model":"cx/gpt-5.6-luna","prompt_sha256":"4786e6f3681b05b0e475e188f0fbd61e98def58906b98ae8010b07dfd44df596","output_schema_sha256":"0386bc6702386f87d7595f5a50c63b60d2fa20f22b58ef050ea6677616e6d1d8","schema_id":"chart_extraction","stage1_visual_type":"plot","prompt_task_sha256":"1dd7985b1567eda8d66c3da3478eab188eb6764f7e1445eb1b1014b72ad08dd6","route_policy_sha256":"897498afc82f7598dc9ebd6687dba16a821e18722262df3e299e45136eed1940","model_binding_sha256":"01208a249b295331443fdc61a0e35c1fe80cfdaea164f7a8d95c94b82517f43c","input_sha256":"d737ba0bf5dd124c733a1f2eee65ccdf2bc6b70dd1fe18a865b3095e6b2ce626","output_sha256":"4ac1983d90e71bc8921559ea634dc89de9dd821fa97e353f47ab816274b1a9b8","input_tokens":2564,"output_tokens":839,"latency_ms":16860},"typed_payload":null,"authoritative":false,"import_eligible":false}